# Monitor: two-tier collection gating

Sparse `@fast`/`@full` rows are not enough — **slow keys must be skipped at collection time** when the phase is `COLLECT_FAST_ONLY`.

## Central gate (required)

- **`stats_set` / `stats_inc`** in `stats.c` must call `collect_tier_key_active()` before storing. Do not add per-collector one-offs when this path covers the emit.
- **`str_collect_key_list` / `str_collect_prefix_key_list`** must honor `collect_set_key_active_hook` (same pattern as `path_collect_*`).
- **`host_key_alias_emit`** relies on `stats_set` — no separate gate needed once `stats.c` is correct.

## Daemon / runtime

- **`stats_runtime_collect_phase_for_tick`**: when `!collect_tier_enabled()`, set phase `COLLECT_FULL` and return without slow-slot math.
- **`monitor_daemon_last_slow_slot`**: reset to `-1` on **SIGHUP** so `sample_freq_slow` reload gets a clean boundary.
- **`write_hdr=1`**: always force `COLLECT_FULL` before collect (schema/`$` invariant).

## Tests

- `g_slow_tier_enabled` defaults **off** in `collect_tier.c`. Any test of phase scheduling or `stats_set` gating must call **`collect_tier_set_enabled(1)`** in Arrange (and reset in teardown if needed).
- Add/extend **`test_stats_set_tier_gate.c`** when changing gating — assert slow keys are not stored on `COLLECT_FAST_ONLY`.
- Tier-disabled path: phase stays `COLLECT_FULL`, `last_slow_slot` unchanged.

